From e2bde93f0ffca7d5cc906020050388726896586e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:08:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the Fabric API mod id in fabric.mod.json (1.0.1)

The release jar declared "fabric": ">=0.165.0" in depends. Fabric API's mod
id is "fabric-api" and Loader has no builtin mod called "fabric" (only
fabricloader, minecraft and java), so the dependency could never be
satisfied. Every install aborted with:

    Mod 'Discord Voice Bridge' (discord_voice_bridge) 1.0.0 requires
    version 0.165.0 or later of fabric, which is missing!

Nesting Fabric API in 1.0.0 worked - the aggregate jar is in META-INF/jars
and listed in the jar's "jars" array - but nesting cannot satisfy a
dependency on a mod id that does not exist, which is why PR #1 did not fix
the report and why installing Fabric API by hand does not either.

- fabric.mod.json: fabric -> fabric-api (>=0.165.0)
- version 1.0.1 so a stale 1.0.0 download is identifiable
- scripts/verify_release_jar.py: opens the built jar, follows nested jars
  recursively and checks every depends entry against the ids/versions that
  are actually present; CI runs it before uploading the artifact
- loader-smoke workflow (manual) boots a real 26.3 Fabric server with only
  this jar to reproduce/confirm the report end to end
- tick handler: guard the SVC plugin, which is null when SVC is absent
- docs: exact supported Minecraft/Loader/Java/SVC/Fabric API versions,
  installation steps, and a troubleshooting table for Loader's messages
